{
  "suite": "features/optimistic-entitlement-projection",
  "version": 3,
  "notes": [
    "Descriptors carry RAW signed-descriptor fields (featureId, featureExternalId, allowanceType, allowance); runners must derive allowance classification themselves (nil allowanceType = boolean; 'fixed' and 'unlimited' are balance-bearing).",
    "Each case drives ONE reactive feature-info instance through its transitions in order; transitions may replace evidence and descriptors to express acknowledgement, revocation, and descriptor changes.",
    "externalPurchaseDeclarations is an input runners MUST consume and MUST NOT derive any overlay from: external billing produces no verified evidence and therefore no projection.",
    "expectedOverlay omitted means the derived projection must be absent (nil), never empty.",
    "Descriptor allowances for retained evidence are pinned at purchase time; the arrival case models cached descriptors becoming available, never an in-place allowance swap."
  ],
  "cases": [
